Sign up, sign in and query your firmfact workspaces from the command line.

Usage:
  ff [command]

Commands:
  ask         Ask a question about a workspace in plain English
  call        Call any server tool by name, with --arg key=value for each argument
  claim       Make a short name such as ff run this CLI
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  config      Show or change CLI settings and profiles
  doctor      Check this installation, the connection and your sign-in
  help        Help about any command
  login       Sign in through your browser
  logout      Sign out: end the session on the server and forget it here
  open        Open firmfact in your browser
  signup      Create a firmfact account
  tools       List or refresh the workspace commands
  update      Update this CLI to the latest release
  upload      Upload invoices, contracts and other documents for firmfact to read
  version     Show this CLI's version and build, and the latest release
  whoami      Show who you are signed in as
  workspaces  List workspaces, choose the default one or check on a setup

Workspace commands:
  none for this host yet; `ff login` or `ff tools refresh` fetches them

Flags:
      --debug              log each request and answer on stderr, with secrets redacted (or set FIRMFACT_DEBUG=1)
      --format format      output format: table, json, csv or tsv (default: table; csv and tsv print a workspace command's rows)
  -h, --help               help for ff
      --host string        Firmfact host (default: FIRMFACT_HOST, else the profile's, else https://firmfact.com); localhost:<port> for local development
      --insecure-http      allow plain http to a host other than this machine (your token travels unencrypted)
      --jq expression      filter the JSON output with a jq expression, such as '.data[].name'; implies --json
      --json               print machine-readable JSON (the same as --format json)
      --profile string     profile to use, one that exists (default: FIRMFACT_PROFILE, else the current profile)
      --timeout duration   limit for each request, such as 90s (default: 60s, 90s for workspace commands and 5m for a chat, and 30s for the server to start answering; or set FIRMFACT_TIMEOUT)
  -v, --version            version for ff
      --workspace string   workspace id or name (default: FIRMFACT_WORKSPACE, else the profile's workspace)

Additional help topics:
  ff environment Environment variables that set the host, profile, workspace and more

Use "ff [command] --help" for more information about a command.
